{
  "duration": 77.799,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.679,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.279,
      "end": 3.439,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.019,
      "end": 5.559,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.039,
      "end": 6.559,
      "text": "two cars"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.019,
      "end": 8.319,
      "text": "start from two towns"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.88,
      "end": 10.939,
      "text": "which are three hundred thirty kilometers apart."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.699,
      "end": 14.559,
      "text": "The speed of the first car is fifty kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.299,
      "end": 17.739,
      "text": "The speed of the second car is sixty kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.239,
      "end": 19.939,
      "text": "Also, both the cars are moving"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.399,
      "end": 21.239,
      "text": "towards each other."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.779,
      "end": 27.639,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find after how many hours they will meet. Now, let us understand one important concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.059,
      "end": 33.759,
      "text": "When two objects move towards each other, the distance between them keeps reducing from both sides. So in this case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.119,
      "end": 35.739,
      "text": "we do not subtract the speeds,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.119,
      "end": 36.659,
      "text": "we add them."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.959,
      "end": 43.479,
      "text": "And we add the speeds only because both the cars are moving towards each other. Got it? Perfect. Now we know the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.979,
      "end": 46.479,
      "text": "Relative speed is equal to the sum of their speeds."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.02,
      "end": 47.919,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.419,
      "end": 52.139,
      "text": "relative speed is equal to fifty plus sixty."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.699,
      "end": 53.619,
      "text": "This gives us one hundred"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.159,
      "end": 55.499,
      "text": "ten kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.059,
      "end": 59.139,
      "text": "Now that we know the relative speed, we can find the time taken to meet."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.559,
      "end": 60.479,
      "text": "We know the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.959,
      "end": 63.659,
      "text": "Time is equal to distance divided by relative speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.159,
      "end": 65.159,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.5,
      "end": 68.699,
      "text": "time is equal to three hundred thirty divided by one hundred ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.379,
      "end": 71.259,
      "text": "After simplifying this, we get three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.58,
      "end": 74.619,
      "text": "So the two cars will meet after three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.139,
      "end": 77.799,
      "text": "Hence, the correct answer is option A."
    }
  ],
